SUMMARY:A Simple Machine
DTSTART:20261114T023000Z
DTEND:20261114T042500Z
DTSTAMP:20261114T023000Z
UID:nQ8QBIoaGe
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 100 mins (1h40m)\n\nSeattle Film Critics Society PNW
  Awards 2026Coming out of the pandemic\, an idealistic but indecisive youn
 g man makes a series of radical choices to get himself out of debt without
  telling his girlfriend-practically fiancée that he’s going to be homel
 ess. Director Mark Alan Hoffman and author Evan P. Schneider scheduled to
  attend\, with post-film Q&A moderated by film critic Mike Ward (Should I 
 See It).\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/seattle-film-critics-
 society-pnw-awards-2026/a-simple-machine\n\nEstimated start: 18:45
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
